OL,3,AWhat we know about the US ground stop
OL,4,Aand what to do if you're affected
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe US Federal Aviation Administration
OL,7,Fhas lifted the longest nationwide
OL,8,Fground stop of flights since the 11
OL,9,FSeptember 2001 terrorist attacks.
OL,11,FThe FAA said Friday's stoppage, which
OL,12,Flasted more than four hours, was "due
OL,13,Fto extraordinary circumstances" from a
OL,14,Fcommunication issue affecting all air
OL,15,Ftraffic control centres.
OL,17,FHomeland Security Secretary Markwayne
OL,18,FMullin said there was no indication of
OL,19,Fa cyber-attack and that everybody was
OL,20,Fsafe.
OL,22,FHere's what we know.
OL,23,APub: 14-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG9/38
